= Field notes

A blank page is a little room for a new idea. *Make space for the thought*, then _find the words_.

== Collect the fragments

The morning was quiet: rain on the window, coffee on the desk, and a sentence waiting to happen.

=== Next steps

- Keep the detail that makes the scene feel alive.
- Leave a little room for a surprising ending.

== Give ideas a shape

#table(
  columns: 3,
  [*Idea*], [*Next step*], [*Status*],
  [A morning walk], [Write the first scene], [Draft],
  [The rooftop garden], [Follow the light], [Outline],
)

== Keep the meaning

Small notes can become something larger. Explore #link("https://typst.app")[Typst], or add a footnote when a thought needs more room. #footnote[This is an imaginary notebook. All you need is a first sentence.]
